<!--
	One live region, mounted once in the shell and present from first paint.
	A live region created at the moment a message arrives is a live region the
	screen reader has not been watching, so the first message — usually the
	only one that matters — is silently dropped.

	It is polite rather than assertive: a toast reports something that already
	happened, and interrupting whatever the person is reading to say "saved" is
	the wrong trade. Anything that must interrupt is not a toast.
-->
<div
	class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-50 flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-4 sm:items-end"
	role="status"
	aria-live="polite"
